  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 appears to interact with Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are involved in the regulation of histone modification. The evidence suggests that palmarumycin CP18 acts as a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, a compound that is itself a target of palmarumycin CP18. This creates a chain of interactions where palmarumycin CP18 indirectly influences the activity of the histone methyltransferase enzyme. The presence of multiple pathways converging on this enzyme supports the idea that palmarumycin CP18 may modulate histone modification through a complex network of molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the enzyme's role in the regulation of gene expression, potentially through the modification of histone proteins, which in turn affects the chromatin structure and function.",
